  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 101 PM EDT Wed Oct 28 2026\n\nThe next few days will remain dry with pleasant temperatures as a\n850-700 mb ridge will be parked across the Southeast. The main\nimpacts through Friday will be morning fog, which should mainly be\nfocused along area rivers and lakes. Low afternoon RH values in\nthe 30s will be a concern to fire weather interests, but winds\nwill be light through the weekend.\n\nPrevious forecasts have pointed to the next chance of rain \narriving Saturday night and continuing into Sunday. Models are \nbacking away from that solution with the latest runs, particularly\nthe ECMWF, which now has completely dry weather until late next \nweek. A few mid/upper level shortwave troughs cross the area in\nthis time frame, but are too moisture-starved in the low levels to\nproduce much measurable precip. The strong 850 mb ridge remains \nanchored to the Mid-Atlantic coast and Outer Banks region through \nearly next week, keeping deep moisture well to our west. We can \ncertainly use some rain, but mostly sunny skies and highs in the \n70s will be enjoyable as we head into November.",
